{% extends "../../_form.njk" %}
{% set title = case.name.forename + " is not eligible to use online check ins"  %}
{% set pageTitleText = "The person is not eligible to use online check ins" %}
{% set pageTitle = makePageTitle({
  pageHeading: [pageTitleText]
}) %}
{% set back = back if back else '' %}
{# Every other reason came from an answer given on the eligibility check, so going back there is a
   real way to revisit it. None of the tier statuses is an answer - the check would rule the person
   out again the moment it loaded, looping straight back here - so the link leads to the case
   overview instead. Checking again once a final Tier has been assigned means starting the setup
   afresh. An absent supervision package and being in the final third are not answers either: both
   come from the ESUP API and rule the person out before the check even renders, so going back would
   loop the same way. Early engagement does come back here, since it only rules the person out
   alongside the accredited programme box - unticking that is a real way to revisit it. #}
{% set returnToOverviewPage = missingTier or provisionalTier or notSupervised or noSupervisionPackage or inFinalThird %}
{% set backLink = '/case/' + crn if returnToOverviewPage else '/case/' + crn + '/appointments/' + id + '/check-in/eligibility-check' %}
{% set buttonText = "Go to " + case.name.forename + "'s overview" %}


{# `reason` completes the sentence below. When more than one fact ruled the person out they arrive as
   `reasonBullets` and are listed instead, with `reason` introducing them - and it is empty where the
   facts are whole clauses in themselves, giving "This is because Joe:". The reasons and the rules
   that pick between them live in utils/eligibilityRules - nextAfterEligibilityCheck and
   nextAfterPilotCheck. #}

{% block form %}
    {# The tier statuses are the reasons that are about the record rather than the person, so they read
       "they" and explain what the status means, in place of both the named sentence above and the
       standard invitation below. A score is either missing or NOT_SUPERVISED, never both, so only
       their order against `provisionalTier` matters - and both win, as they do in the controller,
       since a person with no score at all or no supervision has no Tier to call provisional.
       Not being supervised is the one status that cannot clear, so it offers what might explain it
       rather than inviting the practitioner to check again. #}
    {% if notSupervised %}
        <p class="govuk-body" data-qa="notSupervised">This is because they are not currently being supervised.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">This could be because they have:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet" data-qa="notSupervisedReasons">
            <li>passed away</li>
            <li>been recalled to prison</li>
            <li>have finished their probation</li>
        </ul>
    {% elif missingTier %}
        <p class="govuk-body" data-qa="missingTier">This is because they have not been assigned a Tier yet.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">They will be assigned a Tier once their risk scores have been completed and the system has calculated their Tier. You can come back and check eligibility again.</p>
    {% elif provisionalTier %}
        <p class="govuk-body" data-qa="provisionalTier">This is because they are currently in a provisional Tier.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">They will be assigned a Tier once their risk scores have been completed and the system has calculated their final Tier. You can come back and check eligibility again. </p>
    {% elif reasonBullets and reasonBullets | length %}
        <p class="govuk-body">This is because {{case.name.forename}}{{ " " + reason if reason }}:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet" data-qa="reasonBullets">
            {% for bullet in reasonBullets %}
                <li>{{ bullet }}</li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">If you think this information is wrong, you can go back and check eligibility again.</p>
    {% else %}
        <p class="govuk-body">This is because {{case.name.forename}} {{reason}}.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">If you think this information is wrong, you can go back and check eligibility again.</p>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
